# --- Automated-test database ------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to .env.test (gitignored) and fill in the connection string.
# ONLY test code reads it: scripts/lib/testdb.js gives every test suite its own
# throw-away database on this server. The application itself never loads this
# file and never connects to it.
#
# The bundled local option is the disposable cluster that
#   npm run test:pg:up
# initializes under %USERPROFILE%\.ticketing-test-pg — PostgreSQL on
# 127.0.0.1:5433, loopback only, completely separate from both the installed
# PostgreSQL service (port 5432) and the Supabase production database.
#
# Rules enforced by scripts/lib/testdb.js:
#   - Supabase hosts are refused as TEST_DATABASE_URL (production safety).
#   - Any other non-loopback host needs ALLOW_REMOTE_TEST_DATABASE=1 set below,
#     as an explicit acknowledgement that destructive test resets are OK there.
TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:<password>@127.0.0.1:5433/ticketing_test"

# Uncomment ONLY if TEST_DATABASE_URL deliberately points at a remote,
# non-Supabase PostgreSQL server dedicated to tests:
# ALLOW_REMOTE_TEST_DATABASE=1
